<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Javier Solana</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. 1942</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Javier Solana is a Spanish Socialist politician who was Secretary General of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> from 1995 to 1999 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a>'s High Representative for foreign and security policy from 1999 to 2009. In that role he brokered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belgrade">Belgrade</a> Agreement of 2002, which kept <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> and Montenegro together as a loose union.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/javier-solana.jpg" alt="Javier Solana" width="320" height="475" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: DoD photo by R. D. Ward · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Javier_Solana_1999.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
